file mycelium/README.md the three unreachable modules named, six sentences turned affirmative-first with claims held exactly, and 87 non-ASCII characters swept -- it was seated `20260813`, three days before ASCII-first
file tools/m/mycelium_map_roster_witness.rish the 41st standing guard -- four readings gated at zero, both directions proven, the suffix rule read from the page rather than recited
file tools/fixtures/mycelium_map_roster_scan.sh reads bases, suffixes and modules from the tree; counts symlinks, since a seam symlink is a module a reader meets in `ls`; publishes corpus size beside the verdict
file tools/fixtures/mycelium_map_roster_control.sh fifteen behaviors on real directories in a throwaway pen -- eight refusals bitten, seven honest readings free, a dropped suffix row and an unnamed middle both proven
file tools/fixtures/prose_register_scan.sh mycelium/README.md joins the DOOR roster, which is what surfaced the 46%
file construction/REDS.md rows %185 and %186 booked and closed; rows %180 and %181 folded to archive as the pin passed its bound twice; the headline span read 186 by measurement
file construction/archive/REDS-the-rule-written-as-arithmetic-rows-180.md the folded row, whole, its body links repointed for the deeper room and the header's left as written
file construction/archive/REDS-the-citation-that-named-nothing-rows-181.md the second folded row, checked for the same depth fault BEFORE staging, which found it
file docs-geode/libraries/README.md regenerated -- 38 rows, the new guard counted
file README.md the generated metrics block regenerated -- 1,669 witnesses over 1,891 modules
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri mycelium_map_roster seated 41st
file construction/ITINERARY.md Tier 1 closed on both doors; the live roster directive corrected from 39 guards to 41; next is docs/CRYPTO.md
recommend keep-going docs/CRYPTO.md at 68,547 bytes is the next front door, and the first question is the one this lap answered by measuring rather than assuming -- whether it is a door a reader enters by or a reference a reader consults, since the two want opposite repairs
